#ASSERT `Under section 10(4), who must sign the consent` `s 10(4)(c) an accounting corporation` EQUALS "at least one director of the corporation"

-- Under section 10(5), is the person appointed as an auditor of the company by the appointment of the accounting firm?
#ASSERT `Under section 10(5), is the person appointed as an auditor of the company by the appointment of the accounting firm` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 10(5), is the person appointed as an auditor of the company by the appointment of the accounting firm` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 10(5), is the person appointed as an auditor of the company by the appointment of the accounting firm` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 10(5), is the person appointed as an auditor of the company by the appointment of the accounting firm` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 10(6), is the person appointed as an auditor of the company by the appointment of the accounting corporation?
#ASSERT `Under section 10(6), is the person appointed as an auditor of the company by the appointment of the accounting corporation` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 10(6), is the person appointed as an auditor of the company by the appointment of the accounting corporation` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 10(6), is the person appointed as an auditor of the company by the appointment of the accounting corporation` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 10(6), is the person appointed as an auditor of the company by the appointment of the accounting corporation` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 10(5) and (6), is the person appointed as an auditor of the company by the appointment of the accounting limited liability partnership?
#ASSERT `Under section 10(5) and (6), is the person appointed as an auditor of the company by the appointment of the accounting limited liability partnership` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 10(5) and (6), is the person appointed as an auditor of the company by the appointment of the accounting limited liability partnership` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part sga1 (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Cases for sga1-seat.l4: what a director, officer or member in the seat would state, and the answer the text gives.
-- Every expected value was decided from the text of the section before the run and is written beside the case; a FALSE is the text saying no, a NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- Arguments are positional, in the order of the question's inputs. A case that ends in NOTHING is a case outside the encoding.

§ `Section 59: restriction on allotment`

-- A director of a public company with a share capital that issued no prospectus on formation asks about the first allotment of shares, planned for 13 January 2026.

-- the statement in lieu of prospectus was lodged on 10 January, exactly 3 days before the first allotment: not barred (text: "at least 3 days before")
#ASSERT `Under section 59(1), is the company barred from allotting shares or debentures` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 13 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- lodged on 11 January, 2 days before: barred
#ASSERT `Under section 59(1), is the company barred from allotting shares or debentures` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 11 1 2026) (Date 13 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no statement lodged: barred
#ASSERT `Under section 59(1), is the company barred from allotting shares or debentures` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 13 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a private company is outside the subsection: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 59(1), is the company barred from allotting shares or debentures` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 13 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a company that issued a prospectus on formation is outside the subsection: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 59(1), is the company barred from allotting shares or debentures` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 13 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- default is made and I am the company
#ASSERT `Under section 59(2), am I guilty of the offence of default` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- default is made and I am an officer in default
#ASSERT `Under section 59(2), am I guilty of the offence of default` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- default is made, but I am neither the company nor an officer in default: this subsection makes me guilty of nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 59(2), am I guilty of the offence of default` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- fine not exceeding $5,000
#ASSERT `Under section 59(2), what is the highest fine I may be sentenced to, in Singapore dollars` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 5000
-- not guilty, so the subsection states no penalty for me
#ASSERT `Under section 59(2), what is the highest fine I may be sentenced to, in Singapore dollars` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- imprisonment not exceeding 12 months
#ASSERT `Under section 59(2), what is the longest imprisonment I may be sentenced to, in months` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST 12
-- no default: no penalty stated
#ASSERT `Under section 59(2), what is the longest imprisonment I may be sentenced to, in months` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a director who knowingly contravenes subsection (1)
#ASSERT `Under section 59(3)(a), am I, as a director, guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a director who knowingly authorises the contravention
#ASSERT `Under section 59(3)(a), am I, as a director, guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a director who did none of the three knowingly: the subsection makes the director guilty of nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 59(3)(a), am I, as a director, guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- allotment 1 March 2026: proceedings commenced on 1 March 2028 are within the 2 years
#ASSERT `Under section 59(4), are the proceedings against me barred by the time limit` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2028) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- commenced the day after the 2 years: barred
#ASSERT `Under section 59(4), are the proceedings against me barred by the time limit` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2028) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- proceedings not for the compensation of subsection (3)(b): not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 59(4), are the proceedings against me barred by the time limit` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 2 3 2030) EQUALS NOTHING
§ `Section 60: the statement in lieu of prospectus`

-- A director asks whether the statement in lieu of prospectus that the company means to lodge meets section 60.

-- all 3 persons signed; form, matters and reports are in order; no adjustments were made
#ASSERT `Under section 60(1), does the statement in lieu of prospectus meet the three requirements of the subsection` 3 3 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- two signed and an agent authorised in writing signed for the third
#ASSERT `Under section 60(1), does the statement in lieu of prospectus meet the three requirements of the subsection` 3 2 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- one named person has not signed and has no agent: the paragraph (a) requirement is not met
#ASSERT `Under section 60(1), does the statement in lieu of prospectus meet the three requirements of the subsection` 3 2 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- adjustments were made in a report and no written statement of the reasons is attached: paragraph (c) is not met
#ASSERT `Under section 60(1), does the statement in lieu of prospectus meet the three requirements of the subsection` 3 3 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- adjustments were made and the written statement signed by the report makers is attached
#ASSERT `Under section 60(1), does the statement in lieu of prospectus meet the three requirements of the subsection` 3 3 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I signed, a statement in it is untrue, and I can prove nothing: guilty
#ASSERT `Under section 60(3), am I, as a director who signed the statement in lieu of prospectus, guilty of the offence of an untrue statement or wilful non-disclosure in it` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I can prove the untrue statement was immaterial: the defence is made out
#ASSERT `Under section 60(3), am I, as a director who signed the statement in lieu of prospectus, guilty of the offence of an untrue statement or wilful non-disclosure in it` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I had reasonable ground to believe, and did believe up to delivery, that the statement was true
#ASSERT `Under section 60(3), am I, as a director who signed the statement in lieu of prospectus, guilty of the offence of an untrue statement or wilful non-disclosure in it` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I had reasonable ground but did not believe it up to delivery: no defence
#ASSERT `Under section 60(3), am I, as a director who signed the statement in lieu of prospectus, guilty of the offence of an untrue statement or wilful non-disclosure in it` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the statement is not untrue in fact but is misleading in the form and context in which it is included: section 4(3) deems it untrue
#ASSERT `Under section 60(3), am I, as a director who signed the statement in lieu of prospectus, guilty of the offence of an untrue statement or wilful non-disclosure in it` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I did not sign the statement: the subsection makes me guilty of nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 60(3), am I, as a director who signed the statement in lieu of prospectus, guilty of the offence of an untrue statement or wilful non-disclosure in it` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I can prove the untrue statement was immaterial
#ASSERT `Under section 60(3), does the section give me, as a director, a defence on these facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- reasonable ground to believe, but I did not believe it up to delivery: no defence on these facts
#ASSERT `Under section 60(3), does the section give me, as a director, a defence on these facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
§ `Section 61: commencement of business`

-- A director of a company about to commence business, or a person contracting with it, asks whether the company may start.

-- allotted cash shares equal to the minimum subscription, directors paid up, declaration lodged by the secretary: not barred
#ASSERT `Under section 61(1), is a company that issued a prospectus barred from commencing business or exercising a borrowing power` TRUE TRUE FALSE 100000 100000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- allotted $1 short of the minimum subscription: barred
#ASSERT `Under section 61(1), is a company that issued a prospectus barred from commencing business or exercising a borrowing power` TRUE TRUE FALSE 99999 100000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no declaration lodged: barred
#ASSERT `Under section 61(1), is a company that issued a prospectus barred from commencing business or exercising a borrowing power` TRUE TRUE FALSE 100000 100000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- money may become repayable for want of a listing permission (paragraph (a)): barred even though paragraph (b) is met
#ASSERT `Under section 61(1), is a company that issued a prospectus barred from commencing business or exercising a borrowing power` TRUE TRUE TRUE 100000 100000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the declaration was lodged but by neither the secretary or a director nor a registered qualified individual: barred
#ASSERT `Under section 61(1), is a company that issued a prospectus barred from commencing business or exercising a borrowing power` TRUE TRUE FALSE 100000 100000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a company with no share capital: the "Where" gate fails, so by the periods ruling (b) the answer is the text's no, not "barred" (first written NOTHING: the run caught it; NOTES.md, finding on the failed "Where" gates)
#ASSERT `Under section 61(1), is a company that issued a prospectus barred from commencing business or exercising a borrowing power` FALSE TRUE FALSE 100000 100000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no prospectus inviting the public was issued: the "Where" gate fails, so by the periods ruling (b) the answer is the text's no; section 61(2) is the one to ask (first written NOTHING; NOTES.md, finding on the failed "Where" gates)
#ASSERT `Under section 61(1), is a company that issued a prospectus barred from commencing business or exercising a borrowing power` TRUE FALSE FALSE 100000 100000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- statement in lieu of prospectus lodged and complying, directors paid up, declaration lodged by a director: not barred
#ASSERT `Under section 61(2), is a public company that issued no prospectus barred from commencing business or exercising a borrowing power` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no statement in lieu of prospectus lodged: barred
#ASSERT `Under section 61(2), is a public company that issued no prospectus barred from commencing business or exercising a borrowing power` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the company did issue a prospectus: the "Where" gate of subsection (2) fails, so by the periods ruling (b) the answer is the text's no (first written NOTHING; NOTES.md, finding on the failed "Where" gates)
#ASSERT `Under section 61(2), is a public company that issued no prospectus barred from commencing business or exercising a borrowing power` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a contract made before the company was entitled to commence business, on 1 March 2026; I ask on 1 February: provisional only
#ASSERT `Under section 61(4), is the contract made before the company may commence business provisional only and not yet binding on the company` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- on the date itself the contract becomes binding
#ASSERT `Under section 61(4), is the contract made before the company may commence business provisional only and not yet binding on the company` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a contract made on or after the date is not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 61(4), is the contract made before the company may commence business provisional only and not yet binding on the company` FALSE (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the company commenced business in contravention and I am responsible for it
#ASSERT `Under section 61(6), am I guilty of the offence of commencing business in contravention of the section` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I am not responsible for the contravention: the subsection makes me guilty of nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 61(6), am I guilty of the offence of commencing business in contravention of the section` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a fine not exceeding $4,000 (and a default penalty of $250)
#ASSERT `Under section 61(6), what is the highest fine I may be sentenced to, in Singapore dollars` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST 4000
-- no contravention: no penalty stated for me
#ASSERT `Under section 61(6), what is the highest fine I may be sentenced to, in Singapore dollars` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
§ `Section 62: varying the contracts referred to in the prospectus`

-- A director of a company that issued a prospectus asks before the statutory meeting.

-- a variation before the statutory meeting that is not subject to its approval: barred
#ASSERT `Under section 62, is the company barred from varying the terms of a contract referred to in the prospectus` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the variation is made subject to the approval of the statutory meeting: the "unless" is met
#ASSERT `Under section 62, is the company barred from varying the terms of a contract referred to in the prospectus` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a contract not referred to in the prospectus or statement in lieu of prospectus: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 62, is the company barred from varying the terms of a contract referred to in the prospectus` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
§ `Sections 62A and 62B: no par value shares and the transitional rules`

-- A member or director asks about the company's shares as the law stands now and about the changes made on 30 January 2006.

-- shares of a company have no par or nominal value
#ASSERT `Under section 62A(1), does a share of the company have a par or nominal value` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a thing that is not a share of a company: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 62A(1), does a share of the company have a par or nominal value` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the amount stood in the share premium account on 30 January 2006: on that date it becomes part of the share capital
#ASSERT `Under section 62B(2), has the amount in the share premium account or capital redemption reserve become part of the company's share capital` TRUE (Date 30 1 2006) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the day before: not yet
#ASSERT `Under section 62B(2), has the amount in the share premium account or capital redemption reserve become part of the company's share capital` TRUE (Date 29 1 2006) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- an amount that did not stand to the credit of either account: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 62B(2), has the amount in the share premium account or capital redemption reserve become part of the company's share capital` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- my liability for calls on money unpaid on shares issued before 30 January 2006 is not affected
#ASSERT `Under section 62B(5), is my liability as a shareholder for calls on the unpaid money affected by the shares ceasing to have a par value` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- shares issued on or after that date: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 62B(5), is my liability as a shareholder for calls on the unpaid money affected by the shares ceasing to have a par value` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- filed on 1 March 2006: before the required date and within 6 months of 30 January 2006
#ASSERT `Under section 62B(7), may the company file the notice of its share capital` (Date 1 3 2006) (Date 1 12 2006) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- filed after the 6 months and the Registrar allowed no longer period
#ASSERT `Under section 62B(7), may the company file the notice of its share capital` (Date 1 12 2006) (Date 1 6 2007) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST FALSE
