-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part sgc1 (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Cases for sgc1-seat.l4: every question is asked with the facts of the matching layer-1 test, and the expected value is the one written there from the text.
-- For each question: one case for each different answer its rule gives in the layer-1 tests (a yes, the text's own no, and, where the rule can answer it, NOTHING: a case the text does not cover).
-- A question whose rule never answers NOTHING has no not-covered case; NOTES.md lists them.

§ `Section 199: accounting records and systems of control`

-- Under section 199(1), has my company caused its accounting and other records to be kept as the subsection requires?
-- all three limbs: JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 199(1), has my company caused its accounting and other records to be kept as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- each limb missing in turn: JUST FALSE ("must cause to be kept such records as will sufficiently explain ..., enable true and fair financial statements ... and be conveniently and properly audited")
#ASSERT `Under section 199(1), has my company caused its accounting and other records to be kept as the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 199(2), what is the last day of the period for which my company must retain its records?
-- the period ends 5 years after the end of the financial year: 31 December 2020 -> 31 December 2025
#ASSERT `Under section 199(2), what is the last day of the period for which my company must retain its records` (Date 31 12 2020) EQUALS Date 31 12 2025
-- the end of the financial year falls on 29 February 2020: 5 years later has no 29 February, so P4 gives 28 February 2025
#ASSERT `Under section 199(2), what is the last day of the period for which my company must retain its records` (Date 29 2 2020) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025

-- Under section 199(2), must my company still retain its records on the day I ask about?
#ASSERT `Under section 199(2), must my company still retain its records on the day I ask about` (Date 31 12 2020) (Date 31 12 2020) EQUALS NOTHING
-- both sides of the end of the period
#ASSERT `Under section 199(2), must my company still retain its records on the day I ask about` (Date 31 12 2020) (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 199(2), must my company still retain its records on the day I ask about` (Date 31 12 2020) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 199(2A), must my company devise and maintain a system of internal accounting controls?
-- a private company that is not a subsidiary of a public company: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 199(2A), must my company devise and maintain a system of internal accounting controls` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 199(2A), must my company devise and maintain a system of internal accounting controls` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Under section 199(2A), has my company devised and maintained the system of internal accounting controls the subsection requires?
-- outside the class of companies: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 199(2A), has my company devised and maintained the system of internal accounting controls the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- compliance: public, system maintained, both assurances
#ASSERT `Under section 199(2A), has my company devised and maintained the system of internal accounting controls the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no system
#ASSERT `Under section 199(2A), has my company devised and maintained the system of internal accounting controls the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 199(3), are my company's records kept as the subsection requires?
#ASSERT `Under section 199(3), are my company's records kept as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- neither place
#ASSERT `Under section 199(3), are my company's records kept as the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 199(3), must my company's records be open to my inspection?
#ASSERT `Under section 199(3), must my company's records be open to my inspection` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 199(3), must my company's records be open to my inspection` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Under section 199(4), must my company send statements and returns to a place in Singapore and keep them there?
#ASSERT `Under section 199(4), must my company send statements and returns to a place in Singapore and keep them there` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 199(4), must my company send statements and returns to a place in Singapore and keep them there` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 199(4), has my company complied with the subsection on records kept outside Singapore?
-- records kept in Singapore: the subsection has no verdict
#ASSERT `Under section 199(4), has my company complied with the subsection on records kept outside Singapore` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 199(4), has my company complied with the subsection on records kept outside Singapore` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 199(4), has my company complied with the subsection on records kept outside Singapore` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 199(5), may the Court order the records to be open to inspection by a public accountant acting for me as a director?
-- a public accountant not acting for a director: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 199(5), may the Court order the records to be open to inspection by a public accountant acting for me as a director` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 199(5), may the Court order the records to be open to inspection by a public accountant acting for me as a director` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "but only upon an undertaking in writing"
#ASSERT `Under section 199(5), may the Court order the records to be open to inspection by a public accountant acting for me as a director` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 199(6), am I guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 199?
#ASSERT `Under section 199(6), am I guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 199` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- default made, but the person is an officer who is not in default
#ASSERT `Under section 199(6), am I guilty of the offence of default in complying with section 199` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 199(6), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction for default in complying with section 199?
#ASSERT `Under section 199(6), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction for default in complying with section 199` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- $10,000 or 12 months (not both), and a default penalty
#ASSERT `Under section 199(6), what is the most I may be sentenced to on conviction for default in complying with section 199` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`s 199(6) penalty` OF 10000, 12, FALSE, TRUE)

§ `Section 201: financial statements and consolidated financial statements`

-- Under section 201(1), are these the financial statements the directors must lay before the company at its annual general meeting?
-- statements for another financial year: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 201(1), are these the financial statements the directors must lay before the company at its annual general meeting` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 201(1), are these the financial statements the directors must lay before the company at its annual general meeting` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Under section 201(2), do the financial statements comply with the Accounting Standards and give a true and fair view?
-- complies, true and fair
#ASSERT `Under section 201(2), do the financial statements comply with the Accounting Standards and give a true and fair view` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no true and fair view: the duty is not met, whatever the departure (the override of (13) goes to compliance with the Standards, not to the true and fair view)
#ASSERT `Under section 201(2), do the financial statements comply with the Accounting Standards and give a true and fair view` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 201(5), must the directors of my parent company lay the consolidated financial statements and the balance sheet instead of complying with subsection (1)?
-- not a parent company: the subsection says nothing of it
