#ASSERT `Under section 207(9), is the auditor in default of the duty to report the matter to the Registrar` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 207(9A): a serious offence is one punishable with at least 2 years' imprisonment where at least $100,000 is involved (section 207(9D)); 99,999 is not enough.
#ASSERT `Under section 207(9A), is the auditor in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister` TRUE TRUE 2 100000 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 207(9A), is the auditor in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister` TRUE TRUE 2 99999 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 207(9A), is the auditor in default of the duty to report the matter to the Minister` TRUE TRUE 2 100000 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 207(10): an officer of a company who refuses the auditor access without lawful excuse; with lawful excuse, no offence; a Part 11A register is outside subsection (5).
#ASSERT `Under section 207(10), is the person guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an officer of a company` `s 207(10)(a) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the company access in accordance with subsection (5)` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 207(10), is the person guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an officer of a company` `s 207(10)(a) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the company access in accordance with subsection (5)` TRUE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 207(10), is the person guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an officer of a company` `s 207(10)(a) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the company access in accordance with subsection (5)` FALSE `s 207(5) a register kept under Part 11A` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Hindering an auditor needs no absence of lawful excuse.
#ASSERT `Under section 207(10), is the person guilty of the offence` `s 207(10) an auditor of a subsidiary corporation` `s 207(10)(d) otherwise hindered, obstructed or delayed an auditor in the performance of the auditor's duties or the exercise of the auditor's powers under section 207` TRUE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 207(10), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction` `s 207(10) an officer of a company` `s 207(10)(a) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the company access in accordance with subsection (5)` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS JUST 4000
#ASSERT `Under section 207(10), what is the most the person may be fined on conviction` `s 207(10) any other person` `s 207(10)(a) refused or failed to allow an auditor of the company access in accordance with subsection (5)` FALSE `s 207(5) an accounting or other record that is not a register` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 208(1): a statement in the course of the auditor's duties, no malice: not liable; with malice, the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Under section 208(1), is the auditor not liable to an action for defamation in respect of the statement` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 208(1), is the auditor not liable to an action for defamation in respect of the statement` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 208A(1) and (2): arguments: the provision exempts or indemnifies; a liability that by law would attach; negligence, default, breach of duty or trust; then (2): defending proceedings; judgment in favour or acquittal; an application; relief granted.
#ASSERT `Under section 208A(1) and (2), is the provision void under the section` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An indemnity for the costs of successfully defending proceedings is let through by subsection (2): not void.
#ASSERT `Under section 208A(1) and (2), is the provision void under the section` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not within either description: the section is silent.
#ASSERT `Under section 208A(1) and (2), is the provision void under the section` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

