-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part sgd (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Cases for sgd-seat.l4, the seat of an individual who is or is about to become a director, a company secretary or a member of a company, or who deals with one.
-- Where a seat question passes its answers straight to one layer-1 rule, its cases are that rule's layer-1 tests restated through the question: each expected value was written from the text
-- (the comment above it says which words decide it) before any run, and is not edited to match the module. Where the question builds a record or a date from plain answers, its cases are written here by hand.
-- A line "-- EXPECT <word>" above a #TRACE would say what the trace must print; this file has no traces: every rule with a breach path is traced in the layer-1 tests files.

-- Names for the choices the questions offer (the modules' own constructors), so that the cases below read as a person's answers.
sgdseat_party_creditor MEANS `s 210(3AA) a creditor of the class concerned`
sgdseat_party_liquidator MEANS `s 210(3AA)(a) the liquidator of a company in the course of being wound up`
sgdseat_party_company MEANS `s 210(3AA)(b) the company, where it is not in the course of being wound up`
sgdseat_party_other MEANS `s 210(3AA) some other person`
sgdseat_pos_director MEANS `s 4(1) "officer" a director of the corporation`
sgdseat_pos_secretary MEANS `s 4(1) "officer" the secretary of the corporation`
sgdseat_pos_anyone MEANS `s 4(1) "officer" anyone else`
sgdseat_pos_receiver MEANS `s 4(1) "officer" a receiver who is not also a manager`
sgdseat_pos_court_liquidator MEANS `s 4(1) "officer" a liquidator appointed by the Court or by the creditors`
sgdseat_inv_all MEANS `s 215(1) the transfer of all of the shares in the company`
sgdseat_inv_class MEANS `s 215(1) the transfer of all of the shares in a particular class in the company`
sgdseat_inv_some MEANS `s 215(1) a transfer of some only of the shares`
sgdseat_who9A_a MEANS `s 215(9A)(a) a person who is accustomed or under an obligation, whether formal or informal, to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of the transferee in respect of the transferor company`
sgdseat_who9A_b MEANS `s 215(9A)(b) the transferee's spouse, parent, brother, sister, son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter or stepdaughter`
sgdseat_who9A_c MEANS `s 215(9A)(c) a person whose directions, instructions or wishes the transferee is accustomed or under an obligation, whether formal or informal, to act in accordance with, in respect of the transferor company`
sgdseat_who9A_d MEANS `s 215(9A)(d) a body corporate controlled by the transferee or by a person mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`
sgdseat_who9A_else MEANS `s 215(9A) someone else`



§ `Companies Act 1967, Part 7: arrangements, reconstructions and amalgamations -- the individual's questions`


§§ `Section 210: compromise or arrangement with creditors, members or holders of units of shares`

-- Under section 210(2), am I a person who may apply to the Court for a meeting to be summoned about a compromise or arrangement?
-- (2)(a): "in the case of a company being wound up — the liquidator"; (2)(b): "in any other case — (i) the company; or (ii) any creditor, member or holder of units of shares of the company".
#ASSERT `Under section 210(2), am I a person who may apply to the Court for a meeting to be summoned about a compromise or arrangement` TRUE `s 210(2)(a) the liquidator of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(2), am I a person who may apply to the Court for a meeting to be summoned about a compromise or arrangement` TRUE `s 210(2)(b)(i) the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(2), am I a person who may apply to the Court for a meeting to be summoned about a compromise or arrangement` TRUE `s 210(2)(b)(ii) a creditor of the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(2), am I a person who may apply to the Court for a meeting to be summoned about a compromise or arrangement` TRUE `s 210(2)(b)(ii) a member of the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(2), am I a person who may apply to the Court for a meeting to be summoned about a compromise or arrangement` TRUE `s 210(2)(b)(ii) a holder of units of shares of the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(2), am I a person who may apply to the Court for a meeting to be summoned about a compromise or arrangement` TRUE `s 210(2) some other person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(2), am I a person who may apply to the Court for a meeting to be summoned about a compromise or arrangement` FALSE `s 210(2)(a) the liquidator of the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(2), am I a person who may apply to the Court for a meeting to be summoned about a compromise or arrangement` FALSE `s 210(2)(b)(i) the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Under section 210(1), may the Court order a meeting of the creditors or members to be summoned about the compromise or arrangement proposed?
-- (1): a compromise or arrangement between a company and (a) creditors, (b) members, (c) holders of units of shares; on the application of a person referred to in (2).
#ASSERT `Under section 210(1), may the Court order a meeting of the creditors or members to be summoned about the compromise or arrangement proposed` `s 210(1)(a) a compromise or an arrangement between a company and its creditors or any class of them` FALSE `s 210(2)(b)(ii) a creditor of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(1), may the Court order a meeting of the creditors or members to be summoned about the compromise or arrangement proposed` `s 210(1)(b) a compromise or an arrangement between a company and its members or any class of them` FALSE `s 210(2)(b)(ii) a member of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(1), may the Court order a meeting of the creditors or members to be summoned about the compromise or arrangement proposed` `s 210(1)(c) a compromise or an arrangement between a company and holders of units of shares of the company or any class of them` FALSE `s 210(2)(b)(ii) a holder of units of shares of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(1), may the Court order a meeting of the creditors or members to be summoned about the compromise or arrangement proposed` `s 210(1)(a) a compromise or an arrangement between a company and its creditors or any class of them` FALSE `s 210(2)(b)(i) the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(1), may the Court order a meeting of the creditors or members to be summoned about the compromise or arrangement proposed` `s 210(1)(a) a compromise or an arrangement between a company and its creditors or any class of them` TRUE `s 210(2)(a) the liquidator of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a creditor applying for a company being wound up is not a person referred to in (2): the application gate fails
#ASSERT `Under section 210(1), may the Court order a meeting of the creditors or members to be summoned about the compromise or arrangement proposed` `s 210(1)(a) a compromise or an arrangement between a company and its creditors or any class of them` TRUE `s 210(2)(b)(ii) a creditor of the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a proposal of some other kind: the "Where" gate fails
#ASSERT `Under section 210(1), may the Court order a meeting of the creditors or members to be summoned about the compromise or arrangement proposed` `s 210(1) a proposal of some other kind` FALSE `s 210(2)(b)(i) the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(1), may the Court order a meeting of the creditors or members to be summoned about the compromise or arrangement proposed` `s 210(1)(a) a compromise or an arrangement between a company and its creditors or any class of them` FALSE `s 210(2) some other person` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 210(3), may the meeting be adjourned on the vote that was taken?
-- Arguments: people present and voting, of whom in favour, value held by those present and voting, value held by those in favour.
-- "approved by a majority in number representing three-fourths in value": 6 of 10 is a majority in number; 80 of 100 is more than three-fourths.
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3), may the meeting be adjourned on the vote that was taken` 10 6 100 80 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- exactly three-fourths in value is read as enough (fork F-210-4): 75 of 100
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3), may the meeting be adjourned on the vote that was taken` 10 6 100 75 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 74 of 100 is less than three-fourths: the "if" gate fails and a grant limited by its own wording answers NOTHING (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12)
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3), may the meeting be adjourned on the vote that was taken` 10 6 100 74 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 5 of 10 is not a majority in number
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3), may the meeting be adjourned on the vote that was taken` 10 5 100 80 EQUALS NOTHING
-- nobody present and voting: no majority
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3), may the meeting be adjourned on the vote that was taken` 0 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 210(3AB), are the conditions for the compromise or arrangement to be binding satisfied?
-- Arguments: the four figures of the vote; the Court has ordered another number; that number; the Court has approved by order.
-- (a) a majority in number, (b) three-fourths in value, (c) the Court's approval by order: all three met
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3AB), are the conditions for the compromise or arrangement to be binding satisfied` 10 6 100 80 FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) not met: not approved by order of the Court
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3AB), are the conditions for the compromise or arrangement to be binding satisfied` 10 6 100 80 FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) not met: 5 of 10 is not a majority in number
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3AB), are the conditions for the compromise or arrangement to be binding satisfied` 10 5 100 80 FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) not met: 74 of 100 is under three-fourths
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3AB), are the conditions for the compromise or arrangement to be binding satisfied` 10 6 100 74 FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "unless the Court orders otherwise": the Court has ordered 4 to be enough; 4 in favour meets it, 3 does not
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3AB), are the conditions for the compromise or arrangement to be binding satisfied` 10 4 100 80 TRUE 4 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3AB), are the conditions for the compromise or arrangement to be binding satisfied` 10 3 100 80 TRUE 4 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 210(3AA), is the compromise or arrangement binding on me?
-- Arguments: who I am; the company is being wound up; the four figures of the vote; the Court has ordered another number; that number; the Court has approved by order.
-- "If the conditions ... are satisfied, a compromise or an arrangement is binding": a creditor of the class, conditions met
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3AA), is the compromise or arrangement binding on me` sgdseat_party_creditor FALSE 10 6 100 80 FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the conditions are not satisfied (the Court has not approved): the text's own "if" says no
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3AA), is the compromise or arrangement binding on me` sgdseat_party_creditor FALSE 10 6 100 80 FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3AA), is the compromise or arrangement binding on me` sgdseat_party_creditor FALSE 10 5 100 80 FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) the liquidator of a company in the course of being wound up is bound; of a company not being wound up the text says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3AA), is the compromise or arrangement binding on me` sgdseat_party_liquidator TRUE 10 6 100 80 FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3AA), is the compromise or arrangement binding on me` sgdseat_party_liquidator FALSE 10 6 100 80 FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) the company, where it is not in the course of being wound up
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3AA), is the compromise or arrangement binding on me` sgdseat_party_company FALSE 10 6 100 80 FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3AA), is the compromise or arrangement binding on me` sgdseat_party_company TRUE 10 6 100 80 FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a person the subsection does not name: not covered
#ASSERT `Under section 210(3AA), is the compromise or arrangement binding on me` sgdseat_party_other FALSE 10 6 100 80 FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 210(4), may the Court grant its approval subject to an alteration or condition?
#ASSERT `Under section 210(4), may the Court grant its approval subject to an alteration or condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(4), may the Court grant its approval subject to an alteration or condition` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 210(5), is the Court's order unable yet to have effect because no copy has been lodged with the Registrar?
-- "has no effect until a copy of the order is lodged with the Registrar"
#ASSERT `Under section 210(5), is the Court's order unable yet to have effect because no copy has been lodged with the Registrar` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Under section 210(5), is the Court's order unable yet to have effect because no copy has been lodged with the Registrar` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 210(5), from what date does the Court's order take effect?
-- not lodged: no date yet
#ASSERT `Under section 210(5), from what date does the Court's order take effect` FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- lodged, nothing earlier specified: "on and from the date of lodgment"
#ASSERT `Under section 210(5), from what date does the Court's order take effect` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
-- lodged on 10 March, the Court determined 1 March and the order specifies it: "such earlier date"
#ASSERT `Under section 210(5), from what date does the Court's order take effect` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2026)
-- the day before the lodgment is earlier; the same day and a later day are not "such earlier date"
#ASSERT `Under section 210(5), from what date does the Court's order take effect` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE (Date 9 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 9 3 2026)
#ASSERT `Under section 210(5), from what date does the Court's order take effect` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under section 210(5), from what date does the Court's order take effect` TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE (Date 11 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

