-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part sgf (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Cases for sgf-seat.l4: the seat layer of ss 216 to 216B, asked from the position of the individual (a minority member above all).
-- Every expected answer below was written from the text of ss 216 to 216B (CoA1967.txt, lines 21698 to 21885) before the file was run,
-- never copied from the encoding's output. A failing assertion is a finding. The argument order is the order of each question's
-- inputs; the people are invented to make the facts concrete (Mei, a minority shareholder; Ravi, a debenture holder).
-- Every question has at least one case; the questions with a NOTHING answer assert the explicit "not covered" value.

§ `Section 216: the personal remedy for oppression or injustice -- may I apply, and on what ground`

-- Under section 216(1), may I apply to the Court for an order on the ground of oppression or injustice
-- Mei is a minority shareholder of a Singapore company and applies to the High Court: 'Any member ... may apply to the Court'.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1), may I apply to the Court for an order on the ground of oppression or injustice` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Mei's late husband was the member; the shares have passed to her by operation of law: s 216(7) applies the section to her as to a member.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1), may I apply to the Court for an order on the ground of oppression or injustice` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Ravi holds a debenture of the company and is not a member: 'or holder of a debenture of a company'.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1), may I apply to the Court for an order on the ground of oppression or injustice` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A member of a company incorporated under an earlier corresponding law: still 'a company' (s 4(1)).
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1), may I apply to the Court for an order on the ground of oppression or injustice` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A person who is none of a member, a transmittee or a debenture holder: the text does not say they may apply (outside the limit, not a no).
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1), may I apply to the Court for an order on the ground of oppression or injustice` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A member of a body that is not a company under the Act: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1), may I apply to the Court for an order on the ground of oppression or injustice` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A member who would apply somewhere other than the General Division of the High Court: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1), may I apply to the Court for an order on the ground of oppression or injustice` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216(7), am I treated as a member of the company for the purposes of section 216 because shares have been transmitted to me by operation of law
-- A member is a member.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(7), am I treated as a member of the company for the purposes of section 216 because shares have been transmitted to me by operation of law` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a member, shares transmitted by operation of law: treated as a member.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(7), am I treated as a member of the company for the purposes of section 216 because shares have been transmitted to me by operation of law` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither: the subsection says nothing.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(7), am I treated as a member of the company for the purposes of section 216 because shares have been transmitted to me by operation of law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216(1)(a), is oppression, or disregard of my interests, a ground for my application
-- The majority has run the company's business and paid itself all the profits, leaving Mei out: a listed matter (s 4(8)(a)), conducted oppressively.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1)(a), is oppression, or disregard of my interests, a ground for my application` `s 4(8)(a) the promotion, formation, membership, control, business, trading, transactions, dealings, property, liabilities, profits, income, receipts, losses, outgoings or expenditure of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The directors use their powers to dilute Mei's shareholding in disregard of her interests: the directors' powers limb.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1)(a), is oppression, or disregard of my interests, a ground for my application` `s 4(8) some other matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A matter off the s 4(8) list and no exercise of the directors' powers: the list is open, so not covered (never a no).
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1)(a), is oppression, or disregard of my interests, a ground for my application` `s 4(8) some other matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A complaint about internal management, but neither oppressive nor in disregard of anyone's interests: the ground is not made out.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1)(a), is oppression, or disregard of my interests, a ground for my application` `s 4(8)(c) the internal management and proceeding of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Beneficiaries under a trust of which the company is trustee (s 4(8)(b)), conducted oppressively.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1)(a), is oppression, or disregard of my interests, a ground for my application` `s 4(8)(b) the identity of the beneficiaries under a trust of which the corporation is trustee, their rights and the payments they have received or are entitled to receive` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same matter where the company is not such a trustee: the paragraph's condition fails; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1)(a), is oppression, or disregard of my interests, a ground for my application` `s 4(8)(b) the identity of the beneficiaries under a trust of which the corporation is trustee, their rights and the payments they have received or are entitled to receive` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216(1)(b), is an act or resolution that unfairly discriminates against or prejudices members or holders of debentures a ground for my application
-- The company has issued shares to the majority only, on terms that unfairly discriminate against Mei: an act, unfair discrimination.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1)(b), is an act or resolution that unfairly discriminates against or prejudices members or holders of debentures a ground for my application` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A resolution proposed that is otherwise prejudicial to the minority: a resolution, prejudice.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1)(b), is an act or resolution that unfairly discriminates against or prejudices members or holders of debentures a ground for my application` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither an act nor a resolution: no ground, however unfair the effect.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1)(b), is an act or resolution that unfairly discriminates against or prejudices members or holders of debentures a ground for my application` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An act that neither discriminates unfairly nor prejudices anyone: no ground.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1)(b), is an act or resolution that unfairly discriminates against or prejudices members or holders of debentures a ground for my application` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 216(1), may the Minister apply to the Court for an order about my company
-- A declared company under Part 9: the Minister may apply.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1), may the Minister apply to the Court for an order about my company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a declared company: the text does not say the Minister may.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(1), may the Minister apply to the Court for an order about my company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 216(2) to (4): what the Court may order, and what follows`

-- Under section 216(2), may the Court make an order to bring the matters complained of to an end or to remedy them
-- The Court has found a ground established on my application and the order is meant to end or remedy the matters complained of: it may make an order, including any order.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2), may the Court make an order to bring the matters complained of to an end or to remedy them` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Court has formed no such opinion: the 'if' gate of the grant fails, so not covered (the text does not say the Court may not).
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2), may the Court make an order to bring the matters complained of to an end or to remedy them` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The order sought is not meant to end or remedy the matters complained of: outside the purpose the grant states; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2), may the Court make an order to bring the matters complained of to an end or to remedy them` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216(2)(a), may the Court direct or prohibit an act, or cancel or vary a transaction or resolution
-- The Court has found a ground established on my application and the order is meant to end or remedy the matters complained of: it may make an order, including (a) direct or prohibit an act, cancel or vary a transaction or resolution.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(a), may the Court direct or prohibit an act, or cancel or vary a transaction or resolution` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Court has formed no such opinion: the 'if' gate of the grant fails, so not covered (the text does not say the Court may not).
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(a), may the Court direct or prohibit an act, or cancel or vary a transaction or resolution` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The order sought is not meant to end or remedy the matters complained of: outside the purpose the grant states; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(a), may the Court direct or prohibit an act, or cancel or vary a transaction or resolution` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216(2)(b), may the Court regulate how the company's affairs are conducted in future
-- The Court has found a ground established on my application and the order is meant to end or remedy the matters complained of: it may make an order, including (b) regulate the conduct of the company's affairs in future.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(b), may the Court regulate how the company's affairs are conducted in future` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Court has formed no such opinion: the 'if' gate of the grant fails, so not covered (the text does not say the Court may not).
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(b), may the Court regulate how the company's affairs are conducted in future` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The order sought is not meant to end or remedy the matters complained of: outside the purpose the grant states; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(b), may the Court regulate how the company's affairs are conducted in future` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216(2)(c), may the Court authorise civil proceedings in the company's name
-- The Court has found a ground established on my application and the order is meant to end or remedy the matters complained of: it may make an order, including (c) authorise civil proceedings in the company's name.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(c), may the Court authorise civil proceedings in the company's name` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Court has formed no such opinion: the 'if' gate of the grant fails, so not covered (the text does not say the Court may not).
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(c), may the Court authorise civil proceedings in the company's name` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The order sought is not meant to end or remedy the matters complained of: outside the purpose the grant states; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(c), may the Court authorise civil proceedings in the company's name` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216(2)(d), may the Court provide for the purchase of the company's shares or debentures by the buyer I have in mind
-- Mei asks that the other members buy her out: the text names other members.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(d), may the Court provide for the purchase of the company's shares or debentures by the buyer I have in mind` TRUE TRUE `s 216(2)(d) another member or holder of debentures of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Mei asks that the company buy her shares: the text names the company itself.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(d), may the Court provide for the purchase of the company's shares or debentures by the buyer I have in mind` TRUE TRUE `s 216(2)(d) the company itself` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A third-party buyer: not on the list, and the list is not closed; not covered (never a no).
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(d), may the Court provide for the purchase of the company's shares or debentures by the buyer I have in mind` TRUE TRUE `s 216(2)(d) some other person` EQUALS NOTHING
-- No finding by the Court yet: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(d), may the Court provide for the purchase of the company's shares or debentures by the buyer I have in mind` FALSE TRUE `s 216(2)(d) the company itself` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216(2)(e), may the Court provide for a reduction of the company's capital where the company buys shares
-- The order has the company buying Mei's shares: it may provide for a reduction of capital accordingly.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(e), may the Court provide for a reduction of the company's capital where the company buys shares` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The other members buy: no purchase by the company, so outside the paragraph's scope; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(e), may the Court provide for a reduction of the company's capital where the company buys shares` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216(2)(f), may the Court provide that the company be wound up
-- The Court has found a ground established on my application and the order is meant to end or remedy the matters complained of: it may make an order, including (f) wind the company up.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(f), may the Court provide that the company be wound up` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Court has formed no such opinion: the 'if' gate of the grant fails, so not covered (the text does not say the Court may not).
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(f), may the Court provide that the company be wound up` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The order sought is not meant to end or remedy the matters complained of: outside the purpose the grant states; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(2)(f), may the Court provide that the company be wound up` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216(3), do the winding up provisions of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 apply as if the company had applied
-- The Court has ordered winding up under s 216(2)(f): the winding up provisions apply as if the company had applied.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(3), do the winding up provisions of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 apply as if the company had applied` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No order for winding up under subsection (2)(f): the 'where' condition is not met.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(3), do the winding up provisions of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 apply as if the company had applied` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 216(4), is the company barred from making a further alteration to its constitution without the Court's permission
-- The Court's order added a clause protecting the minority; the board now wants to delete it without the Court's permission: barred.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(4), is the company barred from making a further alteration to its constitution without the Court's permission` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No order altered the constitution: subsection (4) is not engaged.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(4), is the company barred from making a further alteration to its constitution without the Court's permission` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A further alteration that is not inconsistent with the order: outside the bar's scope; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(4), is the company barred from making a further alteration to its constitution without the Court's permission` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Court has given permission: 'without the permission of the Court' is the bar's own limit; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(4), is the company barred from making a further alteration to its constitution without the Court's permission` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216(4), do the alterations the Court's order made have the same effect as if the company had made them by resolution
-- The order's own alterations have the effect of a resolution of the company.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(4), do the alterations the Court's order made have the same effect as if the company had made them by resolution` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The order made no alteration: the text says nothing about effect.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(4), do the alterations the Court's order made have the same effect as if the company had made them by resolution` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 216(5) and (6): lodging a copy of the order with the Registrar`

-- Under section 216(5), what is the last day for lodging a copy of the order with the Registrar
-- The order was made on 1 March 2027: 14 days after is 15 March 2027.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(5), what is the last day for lodging a copy of the order with the Registrar` (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS Date 15 3 2027
-- The order was made on 31 December 2026: 14 days after is 14 January 2027, in the next year.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(5), what is the last day for lodging a copy of the order with the Registrar` (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS Date 14 1 2027

-- Under section 216(5), have I failed to lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar within 14 days after it was made
-- Mei lodged on 15 March 2027, the 14th day: in time; she has not failed.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(5), have I failed to lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar within 14 days after it was made` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 15 3 2027) (Date 20 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Mei lodged on 16 March 2027, one day late: she has failed.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(5), have I failed to lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar within 14 days after it was made` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 16 3 2027) (Date 20 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not lodged, today is the 14th day: the time has not run out; not yet failed.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(5), have I failed to lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar within 14 days after it was made` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not lodged, today is the 15th day: failed.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(5), have I failed to lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar within 14 days after it was made` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 16 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not the applicant: the duty is the applicant's; this person has not failed to comply with it.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(5), have I failed to lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar within 14 days after it was made` FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 30 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 216(6), am I guilty of an offence for failing to lodge a copy of the order in time
-- Mei never lodged and the 14 days have passed: guilty of the offence.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(6), am I guilty of an offence for failing to lodge a copy of the order in time` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 16 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Mei lodged one day late: guilty of the offence.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(6), am I guilty of an offence for failing to lodge a copy of the order in time` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 16 3 2027) (Date 20 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Mei lodged in time: not guilty of this offence.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(6), am I guilty of an offence for failing to lodge a copy of the order in time` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 15 3 2027) (Date 20 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 216(6), what is the most I can be fined for failing to lodge a copy of the order in time
-- Guilty: a fine not exceeding $1,000.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(6), what is the most I can be fined for failing to lodge a copy of the order in time` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 16 3 2027) EQUALS JUST 1000
-- Not guilty: the subsection states no penalty for her.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(6), what is the most I can be fined for failing to lodge a copy of the order in time` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 15 3 2027) (Date 20 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216(6), am I also liable to a default penalty for failing to lodge a copy of the order in time
-- Guilty: 'and also to a default penalty'.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(6), am I also liable to a default penalty for failing to lodge a copy of the order in time` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 16 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not guilty: no penalty is stated for her.
#ASSERT `Under section 216(6), am I also liable to a default penalty for failing to lodge a copy of the order in time` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 15 3 2027) (Date 20 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 216A: permission to bring or take over a case in the company's name`

-- Under section 216A(1), am I a complainant who may ask the Court for permission to act in the company's name
-- Mei is a member of the company: a complainant under (a).
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(1), am I a complainant who may ask the Court for permission to act in the company's name` TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not treated the person as a proper person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Someone who is not a member and whom the Court has not treated as a proper person: not a complainant.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(1), am I a complainant who may ask the Court for permission to act in the company's name` TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not treated the person as a proper person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A debenture holder whom the Court has treated as a proper person: a complainant under (c).
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(1), am I a complainant who may ask the Court for permission to act in the company's name` TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has treated the person as a proper person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A transmittee who is not a member, the Court not yet having decided: s 216(7) does not reach s 216A; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(1), am I a complainant who may ask the Court for permission to act in the company's name` TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not yet decided` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216A(2), may I apply to the Court for permission to bring an action or arbitration in the company's name, or to intervene in one
-- Mei wants to sue the directors in the company's name: permission may be applied for.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(2), may I apply to the Court for permission to bring an action or arbitration in the company's name, or to intervene in one` TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not treated the person as a proper person` `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Mei wants to take over a company arbitration the directors are not pursuing.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(2), may I apply to the Court for permission to bring an action or arbitration in the company's name, or to intervene in one` TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not treated the person as a proper person` `s 216A(2) to intervene in an arbitration to which the company is a party, to prosecute, defend or discontinue it on behalf of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Some other purpose: outside the four the grant names; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(2), may I apply to the Court for permission to bring an action or arbitration in the company's name, or to intervene in one` TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not treated the person as a proper person` `s 216A(2) for some other purpose` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A stranger the Court has not treated as proper: not a complainant, so the grant does not reach them; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(2), may I apply to the Court for permission to bring an action or arbitration in the company's name, or to intervene in one` TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 216A(1)(c) the Court has not treated the person as a proper person` `s 216A(2) to bring an action in the name and on behalf of the company` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216A(3)(a), what is the latest day on which I can give the directors notice of my intention to apply
-- Mei means to apply on 15 March 2027: she must give notice by 1 March 2027.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(3)(a), what is the latest day on which I can give the directors notice of my intention to apply` (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS Date 1 3 2027
-- Leap year: apply on 10 March 2028, notice by 25 February 2028.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(3)(a), what is the latest day on which I can give the directors notice of my intention to apply` (Date 10 3 2028) EQUALS Date 25 2 2028

-- Under section 216A(3)(a), what is the earliest day on which I can apply to the Court after giving the directors notice
-- Notice given on 1 March 2027: the earliest application is 15 March 2027.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(3)(a), what is the earliest day on which I can apply to the Court after giving the directors notice` (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS Date 15 3 2027
-- Notice given on 22 December 2026: the earliest application is 5 January 2027.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(3)(a), what is the earliest day on which I can apply to the Court after giving the directors notice` (Date 22 12 2026) EQUALS Date 5 1 2027

-- Under section 216A(3)(a), have I given the directors the 14 days' notice the section requires
-- Mei gave all three directors written notice on 1 March 2027 of her intention to apply, and applies on 15 March: 14 days.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(3)(a), have I given the directors the 14 days' notice the section requires` 3 3 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Applying on 14 March 2027: only 13 days after the notice.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(3)(a), have I given the directors the 14 days' notice the section requires` 3 3 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 14 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Only two of the three directors were told.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(3)(a), have I given the directors the 14 days' notice the section requires` 3 2 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The notice did not say she intends to apply to the Court if the directors do not act.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(3)(a), have I given the directors the 14 days' notice the section requires` 3 3 FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A company with one director: notice to that director is notice to 'the directors' (s 4(10)).
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(3)(a), have I given the directors the 14 days' notice the section requires` 1 1 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Under section 216A(3), am I barred from bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, in the company's name
-- All three conditions are met: the bar does not apply (the Court still decides whether to give permission).
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(3), am I barred from bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, in the company's name` TRUE 3 3 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Short notice: barred.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(3), am I barred from bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, in the company's name` TRUE 3 3 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 14 3 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not acting in good faith: barred.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(3), am I barred from bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, in the company's name` TRUE 3 3 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not prima facie in the company's interests: barred.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(3), am I barred from bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, in the company's name` TRUE 3 3 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A common law derivative action, not one under section 216A: the bar does not speak to it; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(3), am I barred from bringing the action or arbitration, or making the intervention, in the company's name` FALSE 3 3 TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216A(4), may the Court make an interim order pending my giving notice because it is not expedient to give it now
-- Mei shows that giving notice now would let the directors dissipate the assets: the Court may make an interim order.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(4), may the Court make an interim order pending my giving notice because it is not expedient to give it now` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- She has not established that it is not expedient: the 'where' condition is not met (split site (ii)).
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(4), may the Court make an interim order pending my giving notice because it is not expedient to give it now` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 216A(5), may the Court make orders or interim orders in the interests of justice when it grants me permission
-- The Court is granting Mei permission: it may make such orders as it thinks fit.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(5), may the Court make orders or interim orders in the interests of justice when it grants me permission` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Court is not granting permission: outside the scope; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(5), may the Court make orders or interim orders in the interests of justice when it grants me permission` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216A(5)(a), may the Court authorise me or another person to control the conduct of the action or arbitration
-- The Court is granting Mei permission: it may make such orders as it thinks fit.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(5)(a), may the Court authorise me or another person to control the conduct of the action or arbitration` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Court is not granting permission: outside the scope; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(5)(a), may the Court authorise me or another person to control the conduct of the action or arbitration` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216A(5)(b), may the Court give directions for the conduct of the action or arbitration by the person authorised
-- A person (Mei) has been authorised to control the action: the Court may give directions for its conduct by her.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(5)(b), may the Court give directions for the conduct of the action or arbitration by the person authorised` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No one has been authorised: the paragraph's named complement is absent; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(5)(b), may the Court give directions for the conduct of the action or arbitration by the person authorised` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216A(5)(c), may the Court order the company to pay my reasonable legal fees and disbursements for the action or arbitration
-- Mei's fees are reasonable and she incurred them in connection with the action: the Court may order the company to pay them.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(5)(c), may the Court order the company to pay my reasonable legal fees and disbursements for the action or arbitration` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The fees are not reasonable: outside the grant's limit; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(5)(c), may the Court order the company to pay my reasonable legal fees and disbursements for the action or arbitration` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The fees were not incurred by the complainant: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(5)(c), may the Court order the company to pay my reasonable legal fees and disbursements for the action or arbitration` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216A(6), must my application for permission be made in a District Court
-- The action is in the State Courts: the application must be made in a District Court.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(6), must my application for permission be made in a District Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The action is in the High Court: subsection (6) does not require a District Court.
#ASSERT `Under section 216A(6), must my application for permission be made in a District Court` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 216B: the members' approval, Court approval to discontinue, and interim costs`

-- Under section 216B(1), is a stay or dismissal of my application or action barred where the only reason is that the members have approved, or may approve, the alleged breach
-- The directors ask for a stay only because the majority of members has approved the breach: barred.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(1), is a stay or dismissal of my application or action barred where the only reason is that the members have approved, or may approve, the alleged breach` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- There is another reason for the stay: outside 'by reason only'; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(1), is a stay or dismissal of my application or action barred where the only reason is that the members have approved, or may approve, the alleged breach` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not a proceeding under section 216A: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(1), is a stay or dismissal of my application or action barred where the only reason is that the members have approved, or may approve, the alleged breach` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216B(1), may the Court take the members' approval of the alleged breach into account in making an order under section 216A
-- The members' approval is in evidence and the Court is making an order under section 216A: it may take it into account.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(1), may the Court take the members' approval of the alleged breach into account in making an order under section 216A` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No such evidence: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(1), may the Court take the members' approval of the alleged breach into account in making an order under section 216A` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216B(2), is a stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution of my application or action barred without the Court's approval
-- The company and the directors want to settle Mei's action privately: barred without the Court's approval.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(2), is a stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution of my application or action barred without the Court's approval` TRUE `s 216B(2) a settlement` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A discontinuance without approval: barred.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(2), is a stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution of my application or action barred without the Court's approval` TRUE `s 216B(2) a discontinuance` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A dismissal for want of prosecution without approval: barred.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(2), is a stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution of my application or action barred without the Court's approval` TRUE `s 216B(2) a dismissal for want of prosecution` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Court has approved: outside the limit of the prohibition; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(2), is a stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution of my application or action barred without the Court's approval` TRUE `s 216B(2) a settlement` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A dismissal for another reason: not on the subsection's list; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(2), is a stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution of my application or action barred without the Court's approval` TRUE `s 216B(2) a dismissal for another reason` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216B(2), may the Court give its approval on such terms as it thinks fit
-- The Court is giving its approval: it may attach terms.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(2), may the Court give its approval on such terms as it thinks fit` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Court is not giving approval: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(2), may the Court give its approval on such terms as it thinks fit` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216B(2), may the Court order a party to give me notice of a stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal
-- The Court determines Mei's interest may be substantially affected: it may order a party to give her notice.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(2), may the Court order a party to give me notice of a stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Court has not so determined: the 'if' gate fails; not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(2), may the Court order a party to give me notice of a stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216B(3), may the Court order the company to pay me interim costs
-- In Mei's action under section 216A: the Court may at any time order the company to pay her interim costs.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(3), may the Court order the company to pay me interim costs` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not a proceeding under section 216A: not covered.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(3), may the Court order the company to pay me interim costs` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 216B(3), may I be made accountable for the interim costs when my application or action is finally disposed of
-- Interim costs were ordered and the action is finally disposed of: Mei may be accountable for them.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(3), may I be made accountable for the interim costs when my application or action is finally disposed of` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not yet finally disposed of: the 'upon final disposition' gate fails (split site (ii)).
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(3), may I be made accountable for the interim costs when my application or action is finally disposed of` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No interim costs were ordered: nothing to account for.
#ASSERT `Under section 216B(3), may I be made accountable for the interim costs when my application or action is finally disposed of` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions from part sge (merged by the lead; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, Part 10A, ss 355 to 364A -- CASES FOR THE SEAT LAYER (sge-seat.l4).
-- Each question is asked with the facts a person in the seat would state. Every expected value was written from the text, beside the case,
-- before the run (never copied from the output). Arguments are in the order the question's GIVEN lists them. Dates used: a company
-- registered on 1 March 2027 (60 days after is 30 April 2027, 30 days after is 31 March 2027), and the other dates each case names.
-- The "not covered" cases assert NOTHING: the text does not say.

§ `Sections 355 and 356: whether Part 10A applies to the body, and the words it defines`

-- Under section 355, does Part 10A of the Companies Act apply to the body I act for
-- a body corporate incorporated abroad that means to register here is within the Part
#ASSERT `Under section 355, does Part 10A of the Companies Act apply to the body I act for` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a body incorporated in Singapore is not a foreign corporate entity, and the section says nothing of it
#ASSERT `Under section 355, does Part 10A of the Companies Act apply to the body I act for` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- an entity with no intention to register here is outside the Part, and the section says nothing of it
#ASSERT `Under section 355, does Part 10A of the Companies Act apply to the body I act for` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 356, is the body I act for a foreign corporate entity
-- a body corporate incorporated outside Singapore is one
#ASSERT `Under section 356, is the body I act for a foreign corporate entity` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "means": a body incorporated in Singapore is not one
#ASSERT `Under section 356, is the body I act for a foreign corporate entity` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 356, what is the date of registration of the foreign corporate entity
-- the date specified in the notice
#ASSERT `Under section 356, what is the date of registration of the foreign corporate entity` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2027)
-- no notice yet, so the text gives no date
#ASSERT `Under section 356, what is the date of registration of the foreign corporate entity` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 356, what is the place of incorporation of the foreign corporate entity
-- an entity that transferred its domicile: where it is domiciled when it applies
#ASSERT `Under section 356, what is the place of incorporation of the foreign corporate entity` TRUE "Cayman Islands" EQUALS JUST "Cayman Islands"
-- the definition is given only for that case
#ASSERT `Under section 356, what is the place of incorporation of the foreign corporate entity` FALSE "Cayman Islands" EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 356, is the foreign corporate entity registered
-- the Registrar has registered an entity that applied
#ASSERT `Under section 356, is the foreign corporate entity registered` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an applicant the Registrar has not registered is not registered
#ASSERT `Under section 356, is the foreign corporate entity registered` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- defined for an entity that has applied
#ASSERT `Under section 356, is the foreign corporate entity registered` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 357: reserving the name of the intended company`

-- Under section 357(1), must the foreign corporate entity I act for apply to reserve the name of the intended company
-- an entity that intends to be registered must apply to reserve the name
#ASSERT `Under section 357(1), must the foreign corporate entity I act for apply to reserve the name of the intended company` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an entity with no such intention is outside the duty, and the text says nothing of it
#ASSERT `Under section 357(1), must the foreign corporate entity I act for apply to reserve the name of the intended company` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not a foreign corporate entity: outside the duty
#ASSERT `Under section 357(1), must the foreign corporate entity I act for apply to reserve the name of the intended company` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 357(2), does section 27 apply to and in respect of my application to reserve the name
-- section 27 applies to an application under section 357(1)
#ASSERT `Under section 357(2), does section 27 apply to and in respect of my application to reserve the name` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- any other application: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 357(2), does section 27 apply to and in respect of my application to reserve the name` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 357(3), does the section bar registration of the foreign corporate entity under section 359(1)
-- the name has not been reserved: the subsection bars registration
#ASSERT `Under section 357(3), does the section bar registration of the foreign corporate entity under section 359(1)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the name has been reserved: the "unless" is met, so no bar
#ASSERT `Under section 357(3), does the section bar registration of the foreign corporate entity under section 359(1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 358: applying to be registered`

-- Under section 358(1), may the foreign corporate entity I act for apply to the Registrar to be registered as a company limited by shares
-- a foreign corporate entity may apply
#ASSERT `Under section 358(1), may the foreign corporate entity I act for apply to the Registrar to be registered as a company limited by shares` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a body incorporated in Singapore is not given the power, and the text says nothing of it
#ASSERT `Under section 358(1), may the foreign corporate entity I act for apply to the Registrar to be registered as a company limited by shares` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 358(2), does the application meet the requirements of the subsection
-- form, manner, particulars, certified copy, constitution, other documents and fee all present
#ASSERT `Under section 358(2), does the application meet the requirements of the subsection` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no prescribed fee: the paragraph is not met
#ASSERT `Under section 358(2), does the application meet the requirements of the subsection` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the entity has no foreign instrument ("if any"), so there is no copy to certify
#ASSERT `Under section 358(2), does the application meet the requirements of the subsection` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Under section 358(2)(b), is the application accompanied as the paragraph requires
-- copy certified, constitution, other documents and fee all accompany it
#ASSERT `Under section 358(2)(b), is the application accompanied as the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the proposed constitution does not accompany it
#ASSERT `Under section 358(2)(b), is the application accompanied as the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 358(3), may the Registrar require me as applicant to furnish further information or documents
-- an applicant can be required to furnish more
#ASSERT `Under section 358(3), may the Registrar require me as applicant to furnish further information or documents` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the subsection speaks of an applicant and says nothing of anyone else
#ASSERT `Under section 358(3), may the Registrar require me as applicant to furnish further information or documents` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 359: registration, the notice of transfer, and deregistration abroad`

-- Under section 359(1), may the Registrar register the foreign corporate entity as a company limited by shares
-- no refusal required, section 358 complied with, and the Registrar thinks fit
#ASSERT `Under section 359(1), may the Registrar register the foreign corporate entity as a company limited by shares` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- section 360 requires refusal: the text bars registration in its own words
#ASSERT `Under section 359(1), may the Registrar register the foreign corporate entity as a company limited by shares` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the Registrar does not think fit: the power is not given and the text says nothing more
#ASSERT `Under section 359(1), may the Registrar register the foreign corporate entity as a company limited by shares` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 359(2), is the registration subject to the condition the Registrar imposed
-- a condition the Registrar imposed binds the registration
#ASSERT `Under section 359(2), is the registration subject to the condition the Registrar imposed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no condition imposed: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 359(2), is the registration subject to the condition the Registrar imposed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 359(3), is the notice of transfer of registration as the subsection requires
-- form, date and all three statements present
#ASSERT `Under section 359(3), is the notice of transfer of registration as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a company that is not private need not state that it is
#ASSERT `Under section 359(3), is the notice of transfer of registration as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not in the prescribed form
#ASSERT `Under section 359(3), is the notice of transfer of registration as the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 359(4), is the Registrar required to issue a certificate of confirmation of registration
-- registered, and the company has applied
#ASSERT `Under section 359(4), is the Registrar required to issue a certificate of confirmation of registration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- registered but no application: the duty arises "upon the application", so no duty yet
#ASSERT `Under section 359(4), is the Registrar required to issue a certificate of confirmation of registration` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not registered: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 359(4), is the Registrar required to issue a certificate of confirmation of registration` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 359(5), is the document conclusive evidence that the foreign corporate entity is registered under section 359
-- a notice of transfer of registration
#ASSERT `Under section 359(5), is the document conclusive evidence that the foreign corporate entity is registered under section 359` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a certificate of confirmation of registration
#ASSERT `Under section 359(5), is the document conclusive evidence that the foreign corporate entity is registered under section 359` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- any other document: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 359(5), is the document conclusive evidence that the foreign corporate entity is registered under section 359` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 359(5), what date of the company's registration does the document conclusively show
-- the date the notice states
#ASSERT `Under section 359(5), what date of the company's registration does the document conclusively show` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2027)
-- any other document: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 359(5), what date of the company's registration does the document conclusively show` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 359(6), what is the last day for submitting the document evidencing deregistration
-- 60 days after 1 March 2027 is 30 April 2027 (31 days to 1 April, 29 more)
#ASSERT `Under section 359(6), what is the last day for submitting the document evidencing deregistration` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 30 6 2027) EQUALS Date 30 4 2027
-- the Registrar extended the period: the last day of the extended period
#ASSERT `Under section 359(6), what is the last day for submitting the document evidencing deregistration` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE (Date 30 6 2027) EQUALS Date 30 6 2027

-- Under section 359(6), has the foreign corporate entity complied with the duty to submit the document evidencing deregistration
-- submitted on the last day
#ASSERT `Under section 359(6), has the foreign corporate entity complied with the duty to submit the document evidencing deregistration` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 30 6 2027) TRUE (Date 30 4 2027) (Date 1 8 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- submitted the day after the last day
#ASSERT `Under section 359(6), has the foreign corporate entity complied with the duty to submit the document evidencing deregistration` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 30 6 2027) TRUE (Date 1 5 2027) (Date 1 8 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not submitted, and the 60 days still run on the last day
#ASSERT `Under section 359(6), has the foreign corporate entity complied with the duty to submit the document evidencing deregistration` (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE (Date 30 6 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 30 4 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 359(7), may the Registrar extend the 60-day period
-- registered and the entity has applied for an extension
#ASSERT `Under section 359(7), may the Registrar extend the 60-day period` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no application for an extension: "on application" is not met
#ASSERT `Under section 359(7), may the Registrar extend the 60-day period` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not registered: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 359(7), may the Registrar extend the 60-day period` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 359(8), may the Registrar waive or modify the condition
-- a condition the Registrar imposed under section 359(2)
#ASSERT `Under section 359(8), may the Registrar waive or modify the condition` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- any other condition: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 359(8), may the Registrar waive or modify the condition` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 359(9), may I appeal to the Minister against the decision
-- aggrieved by a refusal, appealing on the 30th day after the decision
#ASSERT `Under section 359(9), may I appeal to the Minister against the decision` TRUE `s 359(9)(a) the refusal of the Registrar to register a foreign corporate entity under subsection (1)` (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 10 7 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the 31st day: out of time
#ASSERT `Under section 359(9), may I appeal to the Minister against the decision` TRUE `s 359(9)(a) the refusal of the Registrar to register a foreign corporate entity under subsection (1)` (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 11 7 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- some other decision: not one the subsection names
#ASSERT `Under section 359(9), may I appeal to the Minister against the decision` TRUE `s 359(9) some other decision` (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 20 6 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 359(9), is the Minister's decision on my appeal final
-- the Minister's decision on an appeal is final
#ASSERT `Under section 359(9), is the Minister's decision on my appeal final` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- any other decision: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 359(9), is the Minister's decision on my appeal final` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 360: when the Registrar must refuse (only for an applicant who has been, or may be, refused)`

-- Under section 360(1), must the Registrar refuse to register the foreign corporate entity
-- not satisfied that the minimum requirements are met: the Registrar must refuse
#ASSERT `Under section 360(1), must the Registrar refuse to register the foreign corporate entity` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- satisfied on both counts: the duty to refuse does not arise
#ASSERT `Under section 360(1), must the Registrar refuse to register the foreign corporate entity` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 360(2), must the Registrar refuse to register the foreign corporate entity on a ground in the subsection
-- satisfied the intended company is likely to be used for an unlawful purpose
#ASSERT `Under section 360(2), must the Registrar refuse to register the foreign corporate entity on a ground in the subsection` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- satisfied of none of the three grounds: the subsection requires no refusal
#ASSERT `Under section 360(2), must the Registrar refuse to register the foreign corporate entity on a ground in the subsection` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 360(3), may I appeal to the Minister against the Registrar's refusal
-- aggrieved, appealing on the 30th day after the decision
#ASSERT `Under section 360(3), may I appeal to the Minister against the Registrar's refusal` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 8 2027) (Date 14 9 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the 31st day: out of time
#ASSERT `Under section 360(3), may I appeal to the Minister against the Registrar's refusal` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 8 2027) (Date 15 9 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not aggrieved: the subsection names the person aggrieved and says nothing of anyone else
#ASSERT `Under section 360(3), may I appeal to the Minister against the Registrar's refusal` FALSE TRUE (Date 15 8 2027) (Date 20 8 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 360(3), is the Minister's decision on my appeal final
-- the Minister's decision on an appeal is final
#ASSERT `Under section 360(3), is the Minister's decision on my appeal final` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- any other decision: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 360(3), is the Minister's decision on my appeal final` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 361: what registration does`

-- Under section 361(1)(a), is the foreign corporate entity a company as defined in section 4(1)
-- on the date of registration itself
#ASSERT `Under section 361(1)(a), is the foreign corporate entity a company as defined in section 4(1)` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the day before the date of registration
#ASSERT `Under section 361(1)(a), is the foreign corporate entity a company as defined in section 4(1)` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 28 2 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 361(1)(a), how does a provision of the Act apply to the foreign corporate entity
-- a provision that pertains to companies applies from the date of registration
#ASSERT `Under section 361(1)(a), how does a provision of the Act apply to the foreign corporate entity` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 361(1)(a) the provision applies to the entity`
-- the regulations adapt it
#ASSERT `Under section 361(1)(a), how does a provision of the Act apply to the foreign corporate entity` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 361(1)(a) the provision applies to the entity as the regulations adapt, except or modify it`
-- before the date of registration
#ASSERT `Under section 361(1)(a), how does a provision of the Act apply to the foreign corporate entity` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 28 2 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 361(1)(a) the provision does not yet apply to the entity`
-- a provision that does not pertain to companies: the text does not say
#ASSERT `Under section 361(1)(a), how does a provision of the Act apply to the foreign corporate entity` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 361(1)(a) the text does not say whether the provision applies to the entity`

-- Under section 361(1)(b), has the foreign corporate entity ceased to be registered as a foreign company under Division 2 of Part 11
-- a foreign company until the date of registration, and the date has come
#ASSERT `Under section 361(1)(b), has the foreign corporate entity ceased to be registered as a foreign company under Division 2 of Part 11` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- before the date of registration it has not ceased
#ASSERT `Under section 361(1)(b), has the foreign corporate entity ceased to be registered as a foreign company under Division 2 of Part 11` TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 28 2 2027) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 361(2)(a), does the registration of the foreign corporate entity create a new legal entity
-- "does not create a new legal entity"
#ASSERT `Under section 361(2)(a), does the registration of the foreign corporate entity create a new legal entity` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not registered: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 361(2)(a), does the registration of the foreign corporate entity create a new legal entity` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 361(2)(b), does the registration of the foreign corporate entity prejudice or affect its identity or its continuity as a body corporate
-- "does not prejudice or affect the identity of the body corporate"
#ASSERT `Under section 361(2)(b), does the registration of the foreign corporate entity prejudice or affect its identity or its continuity as a body corporate` TRUE `s 361(2)(b) the identity of the body corporate constituted by the foreign corporate entity` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not registered: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 361(2)(b), does the registration of the foreign corporate entity prejudice or affect its identity or its continuity as a body corporate` FALSE `s 361(2)(b) the identity of the body corporate constituted by the foreign corporate entity` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 361(2)(c), does the registration of the foreign corporate entity affect its property, rights or obligations
-- "does not affect the rights of the foreign corporate entity"
#ASSERT `Under section 361(2)(c), does the registration of the foreign corporate entity affect its property, rights or obligations` TRUE `s 361(2)(c) the rights of the foreign corporate entity` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not registered: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 361(2)(c), does the registration of the foreign corporate entity affect its property, rights or obligations` FALSE `s 361(2)(c) the rights of the foreign corporate entity` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 361(2)(d), does the registration of the foreign corporate entity render defective legal proceedings by or against it
-- "does not render defective any legal proceedings"
#ASSERT `Under section 361(2)(d), does the registration of the foreign corporate entity render defective legal proceedings by or against it` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not registered: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 361(2)(d), does the registration of the foreign corporate entity render defective legal proceedings by or against it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 361(2), may legal proceedings be continued or commenced by or against the company after the registration
-- proceedings that could have been brought by or against the entity before registration
#ASSERT `Under section 361(2), may legal proceedings be continued or commenced by or against the company after the registration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- proceedings that could not: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 361(2), may legal proceedings be continued or commenced by or against the company after the registration` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 362: revocation of the registration (only for a company that has not submitted the deregistration document)`

-- Under section 362(1), may the Registrar by order revoke the registration of the company
-- the company has failed to comply with section 359(6)
#ASSERT `Under section 362(1), may the Registrar by order revoke the registration of the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no such failure: the power is not given and the text says nothing more
#ASSERT `Under section 362(1), may the Registrar by order revoke the registration of the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 362(2), has the Registrar done what the subsection requires before making an order of revocation
-- written notice, 30 days for representations, none made
#ASSERT `Under section 362(2), has the Registrar done what the subsection requires before making an order of revocation` TRUE 30 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a notice giving 29 days is not what the subsection requires
#ASSERT `Under section 362(2), has the Registrar done what the subsection requires before making an order of revocation` TRUE 29 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- representations made but not considered
#ASSERT `Under section 362(2), has the Registrar done what the subsection requires before making an order of revocation` TRUE 30 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 362(3), may the Registrar order that the registration of the company be revoked
-- the day after the 30 days have expired and no cause shown
#ASSERT `Under section 362(3), may the Registrar order that the registration of the company be revoked` (Date 1 3 2027) 30 (Date 1 4 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the 30th day: the time has not yet expired
#ASSERT `Under section 362(3), may the Registrar order that the registration of the company be revoked` (Date 1 3 2027) 30 (Date 31 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- cause to the contrary was shown: the "unless" is met
#ASSERT `Under section 362(3), may the Registrar order that the registration of the company be revoked` (Date 1 3 2027) 30 (Date 1 4 2027) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 362(4), has the Registrar published and served the notice of the order of revocation
-- published in the Gazette and served on the company
#ASSERT `Under section 362(4), has the Registrar published and served the notice of the order of revocation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- published but not served
#ASSERT `Under section 362(4), has the Registrar published and served the notice of the order of revocation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 362(5), has the order of revocation taken effect
-- on the day of publication
#ASSERT `Under section 362(5), has the order of revocation taken effect` TRUE (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 10 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the day before publication
#ASSERT `Under section 362(5), has the order of revocation taken effect` TRUE (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 9 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 362(5), has the company ceased to be a company as defined in section 4(1)
-- on the day of publication
#ASSERT `Under section 362(5), has the company ceased to be a company as defined in section 4(1)` TRUE (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 10 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not yet published
#ASSERT `Under section 362(5), has the company ceased to be a company as defined in section 4(1)` FALSE (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 11 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 362(5), have the provisions of the Act ceased to apply to the company
-- on the day of publication
#ASSERT `Under section 362(5), have the provisions of the Act ceased to apply to the company` TRUE (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 10 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the day before publication
#ASSERT `Under section 362(5), have the provisions of the Act ceased to apply to the company` TRUE (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 9 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 362(6), is the order of revocation final
-- an order of revocation under section 362(3) is final
#ASSERT `Under section 362(6), is the order of revocation final` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- any other order: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 362(6), is the order of revocation final` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 362(7), does my liability continue despite the order of revocation
-- an officer with a liability in respect of the company
#ASSERT `Under section 362(7), does my liability continue despite the order of revocation` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a member with a liability in respect of the company
#ASSERT `Under section 362(7), does my liability continue despite the order of revocation` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- neither an officer nor a member: the subsection names them and says nothing of anyone else
#ASSERT `Under section 362(7), does my liability continue despite the order of revocation` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 362(8), does section 362 prejudice the enforcement of the right or claim
-- "does not prejudice the enforcement by a person of a right or claim against the company"
#ASSERT `Under section 362(8), does section 362 prejudice the enforcement of the right or claim` `s 362(8)(a) the enforcement by a person of a right or claim against the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- some other enforcement: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 362(8), does section 362 prejudice the enforcement of the right or claim` `s 362(8) some other enforcement` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 363: charges that existed before registration`

-- Under section 363(1), must a statement of the charge be lodged with the Registrar
-- a charge from before registration that Division 8 of Part 4 would have required to be registered
#ASSERT `Under section 363(1), must a statement of the charge be lodged with the Registrar` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a charge Division 8 of Part 4 would not have required to be registered: no statement is required
#ASSERT `Under section 363(1), must a statement of the charge be lodged with the Registrar` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 363(1), what is the last day for lodging the statement of the charge
-- 30 days after 1 March 2027 is 31 March 2027
#ASSERT `Under section 363(1), what is the last day for lodging the statement of the charge` (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS Date 31 3 2027

-- Under section 363(1), has the statement of the charge been lodged as the subsection requires
-- lodged on the 30th day, in the prescribed manner
#ASSERT `Under section 363(1), has the statement of the charge been lodged as the subsection requires` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE TRUE (Date 31 3 2027) (Date 1 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- lodged on the 31st day: too late
#ASSERT `Under section 363(1), has the statement of the charge been lodged as the subsection requires` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 4 2027) (Date 1 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
