-- satisfied, but nobody entitled has applied
#ASSERT `Under section 363(6), may the Court order that the time for registration be extended or that the omission or mis-statement be rectified` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Under section 363(6), may the Court impose the term or condition on its order
-- the term the text itself names
#ASSERT `Under section 363(6), may the Court impose the term or condition on its order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- neither the named term nor one the Court thinks just and expedient: the text says nothing more
#ASSERT `Under section 363(6), may the Court impose the term or condition on its order` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Under section 363(7), does the section apply to the charge as if it were a charge to which Division 8 of Part 4 applied
-- section 134 is one of the four named
#ASSERT `Under section 363(7), does the section apply to the charge as if it were a charge to which Division 8 of Part 4 applied` TRUE `s 363(7) section 134` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- another section: not named, and the text says nothing of it
#ASSERT `Under section 363(7), does the section apply to the charge as if it were a charge to which Division 8 of Part 4 applied` TRUE `s 363(7) another section` EQUALS NOTHING
-- a charge not required to be lodged: the subsection says nothing
#ASSERT `Under section 363(7), does the section apply to the charge as if it were a charge to which Division 8 of Part 4 applied` FALSE `s 363(7) section 134` EQUALS NOTHING

