-- Cases for sgg-seat.l4: for each question, a yes case, the text's no case where the text has one, and a not-covered case where the text has one.
-- Every expected value was written by hand from the text when the layer-1 tests were written (sgg-tests-*.l4) and is repeated here as the answer
-- to the same facts put through the seat's question; the two questions that take a record (sections 365 and 368(1)) have their cases written out
-- in full below from the ten and the fifteen facts. A case line's comment says which kind of case it is.

§ `Section 365`

-- Under section 365, does this Division apply to the foreign company
#ASSERT `Under section 365, does this Division apply to the foreign company` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- yes: a body incorporated outside Singapore that establishes a place of business in Singapore
#ASSERT `Under section 365, does this Division apply to the foreign company` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- yes: a foreign body that intends to carry on business in Singapore
#ASSERT `Under section 365, does this Division apply to the foreign company` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not covered: a body incorporated in Singapore is not a foreign company
#ASSERT `Under section 365, does this Division apply to the foreign company` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not covered: a foreign company that does none of the three things


§ `Section 366`

-- Under section 366(1), is the person an authorised representative of the foreign company
